Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: Cube 2: Sauerbraten
Source: https://sourceforge.net/projects/sauerbraten/files/sauerbraten/2020_11_29/sauerbraten_2020_12_29_linux.tar.bz2
Comment: NOT FREE. Models and sounds from the Sauerbraten 2020_12_29 ("2020 Edition") release
 that Debian's cube2-data does not ship, because their licenses are not DFSG-free (most are
 Creative Commons Attribution Non-Commercial, some "all rights reserved"). Personal and LAN use
 only; this package must not be put in a public repository. The license and readme files of each
 model and sound directory are kept next to its files in
 /usr/share/games/cube2/packages/{models,sounds}/*/ . By directory:
 .
 models/ammo, boost, health, flags, gibs, debris, barreldebris (makkE, Markus Bekel):
 CC BY-NC-SA (at-nc-sa). models/quad: Dietmar "DCP" Pier, converted by makkE.
 models/teleporter: Todretter, skin by makkE, "all rights reserved so far".
 models/hudguns, vwep, mrfixit, inky, captaincannon (John "geartrooper" Siar and others; Mr.
 Fixit textures by Acord, masks by Nieb): CC BY-NC 3.0. models/snoutx10k (Siar): CC BY 3.0.
 models/skull (Jean Ayers, 2012): CC BY-SA 3.0. models/ogro, ogro2: Magarnigal, skins by Ogro_Fix
 and Deranged, ogro2 rigged by Siar (the 1998 Quake II player model's own terms, see
 ogro/Ogro.txt). Other directories keep their own license files.
 sounds: sounds/free and awesund (modified by Darthvim, see Sound.txt), q009 (Slawomir
 "Q009" Blauciak, CC BY-SA), ambience (CC Sampling+, authors.txt), razgriz, drakker, sprite
 (their license.txt), the rest per their README files. See docs/PACKAGING.md in the project for
 the full notes.

